@reswqa the duration that I create with pl.duration(seconds=10) is instantiated as duration with `ns` time_unit. That's the only reason. But it should maintain the original dtype duration with the correct time_unit. 

So this should also work:

```python
result = pl.select(
    pl.sum_horizontal([pl.duration(seconds=10)]).cast(pl.Duration(time_unit='us')).alias('sum_duration')
)


expected = pl.DataFrame(
    [
        pl.Series("sum_duration", [datetime.timedelta(seconds=10)], dtype=pl.Duration(time_unit='us')),
    ]
)
```

